! VFL PACK LOOP ACROSS WORD BOUNDARIES -- reduction of C22-6578 Problem
! 2.6 Method 3's PACK1 loop (decks/problem_2_6_method3.strap), which
! returned only three fields of its answer when bsv/StretchTiming.bsv's
! VFL E-box times were made per-operation on 2026-11-16.  Sixteen 20-bit
! B fields are taken from 24-bit records (4-bit A field skipped) by a
! progressive L and packed by a progressive ST, both of which cross word
! boundaries.
!
! RESULT, hand-derived: ANS is the sixteen B fields end to end,
! 0xB07F0B12F1B2DF2B 30F3B49F4B5FF5B6 4F6B7BF7B81F8B9E F9BA6FABB3FBBCCF
! CBD8FDBE5FEBFAFF.
!
! THE BUG IT PINS.  Progressive indexing's second part sets the index
! result indicators, XCZ among them, when the LEVEL executes (execute()'s
! setIndexResultIndicatorsF(ind, vflPx1), Reference Manual printed p.21).
! iboxHazard treated a branch on an index indicator as I-box-local, so
! BZXCZ ran ahead of the pending ST, read XCZ before the ST had counted,
! and fell through.  An instruction trace of the failing run (temporary $displays): the ST at 2004 was
! loaded at clock 183, BZXCZ at 2006 executed at 198, and the ST was
! removed at 199 -- after the third pass, which is where the answer
! stopped.  Under the old flat VFL times Problem 2.6 Method 3 passed:
! its ST was removed before the branch was reached.
! FIX: an index-indicator branch waits while any pending level is
! progressive (StretchIBox's anyProgressive).
! INJECTION, observed 2026-11-16: without that term the run halts at 214
! clocks, ANS_w0 = 0xB07F0B12F1B2DF20 (three fields and four bits of
! zeros) and ANS_w1..w4 = 0 -- five FAILs and the cycle count, nothing
! else.  With it: all five PASS, 889 clocks.

        SLC, 1000.0
START   LX, $1, XWA; LV, $2, VFD
PACK    L(BU,20)(V+I), 0.24($2)         ! skip A field
        ST(BU,20) (V+IC), 0.20 ($1)     ! store B field
        BZXCZ, PACK
PASS    BEW, $
XWA     XW, ANS, 16, $
VFD     VF, DATA +0.04
        SLC, 1200.0
DATA    DD(BU,64,8), (16)7B07F02B12F1DB2D
        DD(BU,64,8), (16)F20B30F39B49F4FB
        DD(BU,64,8), (16)5FF54B64F6BB7BF7
        DD(BU,64,8), (16)1B81F8EB9EF96BA6
        DD(BU,64,8), (16)FA3BB3FBCBCCFC8B
        DD(BU,64,8), (16)D8FD5BE5FEABFAFF
        SLC, 1210.0
ANS     DRZ(BU, 20), (16)
        END, START
